# Prompt Vault — Agent Project Rules

PROJECT PURPOSE
Build a small personal prompt library for video editors and motion designers.

APPROVED STACK
- React, TypeScript and Vite
- Plain CSS
- Browser localStorage
- No backend, authentication, payments or AI APIs

MVP FEATURES
1. Save prompts with title, category and body text.
2. Search saved prompts quickly.
3. Copy prompt text in one click.
4. Edit and delete prompts.

DESIGN
- Clean, minimal, responsive layout
- Clear visual hierarchy and sufficient contrast
- Accessible keyboard controls, labels and visible focus
- Helpful empty, success and error states

DATA RULES
- Use stable unique IDs.
- Preserve saved data across reloads in the same browser.
- Validate required fields; do not save blank prompts.
- Gracefully handle unavailable or full localStorage.
- Confirm destructive deletion.
- Do not silently erase or overwrite existing records.
- Make it clear that browser storage is device/browser-specific and not a backup.
- Do not include secret credentials in the app.

AGENT WORKFLOW
1. Inspect the current project before editing.
2. Work on only one approved milestone at a time.
3. Explain the plan and files to be changed.
4. Do not add packages or features without a clear reason.
5. Preserve working functionality and unrelated files.
6. Show real verification steps and test results.
7. Report remaining issues and update the progress notes.
8. Ask for approval before destructive operations or deployment.
9. Never describe placeholder behavior as complete functionality.

OUT OF SCOPE
- User accounts and cloud synchronization
- AI prompt generation
- Subscriptions and payments
- Browser extensions
- Collaboration
- Complex category-management systems
